  "id": "COMPOUND:1727 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Castanospermine is shown to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular pathways, with the target enzyme being shared among multiple compounds. The evidence suggests that Castanospermine acts as a modulator of the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn targets DNA polymerase iota. This indicates a potential mechanism where Castanospermine may inhibit DNA polymerase iota through a shared target, possibly by interfering with the enzymatic activity of the sialyltransferase. The presence of multiple compounds that target the same enzyme suggests a possible role for Castanospermine in modulating DNA polymerase iota function, potentially through a common pathway. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Castanospermine may exert its effects on DNA polymerase iota via a mechanism involving the sialyltransferase, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the precise mode of action.",
